From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iio: gyro: Add the Apple AOP gyroscope

The Always-On Processor of Apple A9 devices samples the gyroscope and,
once it has the unit's factory calibration and its batch, raw and
report intervals (EPIC set-property tags 0x16, 0x5c and 0), sends one
motion report (EPIC subtype 0xc1) per report interval. The report is
laid out like the accelerometer's and carries x, y and z in 1/65536
degree per second.

Expose them as an IIO angular velocity sensor: raw values, scale in
rad/s, sampling frequency (the report interval), a software buffer
with timestamps and the standard mount-matrix. The calibration is
complete once the sensitivity and the interrupt calibration are
applied; the range sensitivity and trim calibration are sent when the
bootloader provides them.

[Orchard: from orchard PR #101, commit a54e2049; the gyroscope part of
 drivers/iio/0005, unchanged]

Assisted-by: LLM
